WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.292 --> 00:00:05.585
There is this word

00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.838
that you might have heard
a lot recently, like right now:

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.340
metaverse.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.717
It's suddenly a huge thing.

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:16.179
And while for many people,
it causes a lot of excitement,

00:00:16.179 --> 00:00:18.640
I think it also causes other feelings,

00:00:18.682 --> 00:00:21.810
like confusion and concern.

00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:23.270
And I think that's fair.

00:00:23.311 --> 00:00:25.564
And I’ve also felt confused.

00:00:25.564 --> 00:00:27.315
Metaverse is not really a new thing.

00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:32.487
Many massively multiplayer online games,
for example, can be seen as metaverses.

00:00:32.487 --> 00:00:36.366
And I've certainly also felt concerned,

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:40.078
especially when people talk
about "the metaverse."

00:00:40.537 --> 00:00:44.624
That assumes that there's only
one owner of the metaverse,

00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:49.296
and this owner would get
far too much power and data.

00:00:50.255 --> 00:00:52.257
It also risks being exclusive.

00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:54.384
It might not be accessible for everyone,

00:00:54.384 --> 00:00:57.178
and will risk to introduce
many of the inequities

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.223
we see in the real world in the metaverse.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.726
This was pretty sad to me.

00:01:02.726 --> 00:01:06.479
So then you might wonder like,
why am I here talking about the metaverse?

00:01:06.521 --> 00:01:08.231
That doesn't make sense.

00:01:08.607 --> 00:01:11.693
Well, the thing is, I'm not.

00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:15.196
I'm here to talk about metaverses

00:01:15.238 --> 00:01:19.200
and the vision of how they can provide
a lot of delight to their communities

00:01:19.242 --> 00:01:22.245
and even make the real world
a better place.

00:01:22.287 --> 00:01:25.874
And here we can learn a lot from games.

00:01:25.915 --> 00:01:28.043
So what is even a metaverse?

00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:32.339
How do we create a delightful,
long-lasting metaverses?

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.051
And how can metaverses
make the real world a better place?

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:39.554
And there are, of course,
many answers to these questions,

00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:42.432
and I cannot give you the answer,

00:01:42.474 --> 00:01:45.393
but I can give you one answer.

00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:49.481
If, instead of talking
about the metaverse,

00:01:49.481 --> 00:01:52.609
we talked about thousands
or millions of metaverses

00:01:52.609 --> 00:01:55.820
created by people
from all around the world,

00:01:55.862 --> 00:01:57.822
it would be much more inclusive

00:01:57.864 --> 00:02:00.158
and less risk of toxic uses.

00:02:00.533 --> 00:02:02.786
To me, that sounds quite lovely.

00:02:03.578 --> 00:02:06.039
What I'm showing you right now

00:02:06.081 --> 00:02:09.709
are persistent, endless virtual worlds

00:02:09.751 --> 00:02:12.462
where players can have
lots of fun together.

00:02:12.962 --> 00:02:15.215
They are worlds that connect people.

00:02:15.924 --> 00:02:20.053
Each of these worlds were made
by individuals in Minecraft.

00:02:20.553 --> 00:02:24.557
By removing and placing
their own virtual building blocks,

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:27.686
They could create anything
they can imagine.

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:33.274
And to me, these are creative
and delightful examples of metaverses.

00:02:33.608 --> 00:02:38.446
And I know the power
and the beauty of these worlds

00:02:38.446 --> 00:02:42.283
because I have my own
that's more than ten years old.

00:02:43.118 --> 00:02:45.245
This is my world.

00:02:46.162 --> 00:02:51.209
After many years of playing,
developing, thinking

00:02:51.251 --> 00:02:53.670
and even dreaming about Minecraft,

00:02:53.712 --> 00:02:56.589
I have gained some
experience and learnings.

00:02:56.965 --> 00:03:01.219
Watching our community use the game
in so many different ways

00:03:01.261 --> 00:03:05.140
made me realize how powerful
metaverses can be.

00:03:05.557 --> 00:03:08.810
So I would love to, with these learnings,

00:03:08.852 --> 00:03:11.980
paint a different picture
of what metaverses can be

00:03:12.021 --> 00:03:14.566
if everyone could craft your own.

00:03:14.566 --> 00:03:16.985
And I hope it's a creative,

00:03:17.026 --> 00:03:19.404
fun and inclusive picture.

00:03:19.404 --> 00:03:22.365
In Minecraft, this is one example of this.

00:03:22.407 --> 00:03:25.410
We give the players tools
and endless worlds

00:03:25.452 --> 00:03:29.789
and an infinite amount of building blocks
to have fun and tinker with.

00:03:30.123 --> 00:03:35.420
And with these, the players can craft
their own unique metaverses.

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:38.965
The metaverses, therefore,
belong to the players.

00:03:38.965 --> 00:03:42.385
They do not belong to us, making the game.

00:03:42.385 --> 00:03:44.512
And like, ah, it’s so fascinating,

00:03:44.554 --> 00:03:47.932
because the players are so very,
very creative with the metaverses.

00:03:47.932 --> 00:03:51.227
Some use them to be like,
big cities, castles,

00:03:51.227 --> 00:03:55.190
or like my five-year-old
daughter's recent project,

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.942
an underwater playground for fishes.

00:04:00.111 --> 00:04:04.073
And some players are engineers and build
the most complex machines.

00:04:04.073 --> 00:04:05.700
It's very, very impressive.

00:04:06.117 --> 00:04:09.829
And some prefer to just have
a lovely time with their friends.

00:04:10.497 --> 00:04:12.499
The possibilities are endless,

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.126
and it's up to each player
to set their own goals

00:04:15.168 --> 00:04:18.338
and decide if they want
to create their own metaverse

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:20.298
or join someone else's.

00:04:20.965 --> 00:04:26.805
And it's easier to be creative and connect
with people when you have fun.

00:04:27.138 --> 00:04:29.516
Fun is important.

00:04:29.557 --> 00:04:31.810
And what's more fun than games?

00:04:31.851 --> 00:04:35.355
Within games, we've actually
had metaverses for a really long time.

00:04:35.396 --> 00:04:40.610
Long-lasting games like World of Warcraft
or Eve Online could be seen as metaverses.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.904
And this doesn't surprise me,

00:04:42.946 --> 00:04:46.407
because when we humans
spend time together,

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:49.577
we want to do it in a fun and joyful way.

00:04:49.619 --> 00:04:54.499
And this is true when we spend
time together virtually too.

00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:58.586
Fun means different things
for different individuals.

00:04:58.586 --> 00:05:01.673
Maybe not all of you
want to build fish playgrounds,

00:05:01.714 --> 00:05:04.008
even though that clearly is very fun.

00:05:04.926 --> 00:05:09.347
But this is another reason to why
there should be many different metaverses.

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:13.393
My dream is that there will be a huge
and diverse set of metaverses.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:18.106
Having millions of metaverses
with different strengths and focuses

00:05:18.106 --> 00:05:21.776
enables everyone to find
virtual places they love,

00:05:21.818 --> 00:05:23.027
feel welcome in

00:05:23.027 --> 00:05:25.238
and just can have so much fun in.

00:05:26.447 --> 00:05:30.702
We live in a time where almost everything
seems to depend on statistics,

00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:31.911
metrics and diagrams,

00:05:31.953 --> 00:05:34.455
and we can for sure learn a lot from this.

00:05:34.497 --> 00:05:38.251
But I feel there is a risk
we forget the pure human side,

00:05:38.293 --> 00:05:41.379
the things that excite us,
the things that make us passionate.

00:05:41.838 --> 00:05:43.923
I don't think Tolkien used
metrics and stats

00:05:43.965 --> 00:05:45.592
when he wrote "Lord of the Rings."

00:05:45.633 --> 00:05:49.137
He crafted a universe based on passion,

00:05:49.137 --> 00:05:52.348
vision and delighting his readers.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:55.101
And that’s what metaverse
developers shoul do too.

00:05:55.101 --> 00:05:57.437
We should bring smiles to our place.

00:05:57.478 --> 00:06:01.190
We should develop features
to give this excited,

00:06:01.232 --> 00:06:03.568
butterfly-in-the-stomach feeling.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:09.782
And I hope this is the case
for anyone building metaverses.

00:06:09.782 --> 00:06:12.994
But I must confess, I am a bit worried

00:06:13.036 --> 00:06:15.330
that the main question people will ask

00:06:15.371 --> 00:06:18.583
when they build future metaverses will be,

00:06:18.583 --> 00:06:20.668
"How can we profit from this?"

00:06:21.252 --> 00:06:22.712
That's the wrong question.

00:06:22.754 --> 00:06:28.635
Instead, we should ask
how will our metaverses benefit the users.

00:06:29.218 --> 00:06:30.386
And of course,

00:06:30.386 --> 00:06:34.349
I know that money is important
in this real world we live in.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.810
But the thing is, if players
are super happy long-term,

00:06:37.852 --> 00:06:40.438
that's very likely also related to money.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.148
So everyone can be happy.

00:06:42.815 --> 00:06:45.526
We must focus on taking care
of our communities

00:06:45.568 --> 00:06:48.404
instead of taking from our communities.

00:06:48.905 --> 00:06:53.451
And that goes hand-in-hand
with player trust and thinking long-term.

00:06:53.493 --> 00:06:54.744
Because if you know

00:06:54.786 --> 00:06:58.164
that you can trust that your beloved
metaverse will be around

00:06:58.164 --> 00:07:00.667
and be very much alive for a lifetime,

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:06.214
you feel safe to spend all this time
and all this love on it.

00:07:07.423 --> 00:07:09.300
Look at this amazing world.

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:13.054
It started as a small family project,

00:07:13.054 --> 00:07:15.264
and now, ten years later,

00:07:15.306 --> 00:07:17.892
the family still plays
together in this world.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:22.563
I think this is a great example
of why you should be able to trust

00:07:22.605 --> 00:07:26.734
that your metaverse will be around
and work very well for a lifetime.

00:07:27.402 --> 00:07:30.738
It would be devastating for this family
if they lost this project

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.156
they have together

00:07:32.198 --> 00:07:35.535
and all the dreams
they still hope to fulfill

00:07:35.576 --> 00:07:37.578
in this creative metaverse of theirs.

00:07:38.871 --> 00:07:40.623
As metaverse developers,

00:07:40.665 --> 00:07:45.545
we have a responsibility to keep
people's memories and dreams safe.

00:07:46.337 --> 00:07:47.797
And there's one more thing.

00:07:48.548 --> 00:07:51.634
The virtual worlds
can't reach their full potential

00:07:51.676 --> 00:07:53.970
on making the real world a better place

00:07:54.012 --> 00:07:57.557
if they don't represent
and include everyone.

00:07:57.557 --> 00:08:01.269
Also, everyone deserves
the joy and inspiration

00:08:01.269 --> 00:08:03.479
a lovely designed metaverse can give.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:09.527
Therefore, there need to be metaverses
available and accessible for everyone.

00:08:10.319 --> 00:08:13.489
Each person that wants to,
I will not force anyone,

00:08:13.531 --> 00:08:17.285
should be able to craft
the metaverse of their dreams

00:08:17.285 --> 00:08:20.705
independent of their situation
in the real world.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.835
The in-metaverse economy
should not mirror the inequities

00:08:25.877 --> 00:08:27.128
we see in the real world.

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.381
And it’s much more
delightful and inclusive

00:08:30.423 --> 00:08:35.136
if the resources in the metaverse
are part of a fun and fair game system

00:08:35.136 --> 00:08:39.599
instead of a system
introducing artificial scarcity.

00:08:40.767 --> 00:08:42.810
We also need a variety of metaverses,

00:08:42.852 --> 00:08:46.397
including ones that don't require
expensive devices.

00:08:47.231 --> 00:08:49.150
So when we then have all these, like,

00:08:49.192 --> 00:08:52.403
beautifully designed
metaverses for everyone,

00:08:52.445 --> 00:08:54.822
I mean, on top of all
the joy they will bring,

00:08:54.864 --> 00:08:59.368
we also get many more opportunities
on making the real world a better place.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.371
And I have seen so many beautiful examples

00:09:02.371 --> 00:09:05.541
of how people do that
with their metaverses.

00:09:06.626 --> 00:09:11.089
One that's very dear to me
is the dad who created a minecraft server

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.049
to be a safe and welcoming place

00:09:13.091 --> 00:09:16.260
for his son and other children
on the autism spectrum.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:19.055
This kind of community-created world

00:09:19.055 --> 00:09:21.682
is a great role model
for future metaverses.

00:09:22.058 --> 00:09:26.104
It's a world that welcomes players
that maybe don't always feel welcome

00:09:26.145 --> 00:09:27.313
in the real world,

00:09:27.355 --> 00:09:30.233
and it's a world
that enables these players

00:09:30.274 --> 00:09:32.902
to express themselves in their own ways.

00:09:33.277 --> 00:09:35.738
Family members have witnessed

00:09:35.738 --> 00:09:39.283
how these amazing children
use communication skills

00:09:39.325 --> 00:09:42.203
they learned in the metaverse
in the real world.

00:09:43.913 --> 00:09:47.708
And metaverses can help
charities reach new audiences

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:52.255
and make it more fun and easy
to participate in charity events.

00:09:52.296 --> 00:09:54.423
The World of Warcraft
community, for example,

00:09:54.423 --> 00:09:57.552
raised more than one million dollars
[for] Doctors Without Borders

00:09:57.552 --> 00:10:01.139
to be able to make a difference
in the global response to COVID-19.

00:10:02.014 --> 00:10:03.266
In the metaverses,

00:10:03.266 --> 00:10:05.560
charities can meet people where they are.

00:10:06.394 --> 00:10:11.149
And metaverses can help us communicate
in a common language,

00:10:11.149 --> 00:10:14.193
a language of play, creativity and fun.

00:10:14.652 --> 00:10:17.530
There is an organization
called Games for Peace

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.116
that uses games and their metaverses

00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:22.869
as a neutral playground
to create dialogue,

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.622
friendships and trust between
young people in conflict zones.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:31.127
It wouldn’t even be possible
to bring these young people together

00:10:31.169 --> 00:10:33.504
if not for a metaverse they can meet in.

00:10:34.547 --> 00:10:37.675
And metaverses can help amplify voices.

00:10:38.509 --> 00:10:44.515
Kids in Kosovo used the metaverse
to build their dream neighborhood area.

00:10:45.099 --> 00:10:48.060
By giving the kids millions
of virtual building blocks

00:10:48.102 --> 00:10:50.938
and endless space to build
and collaborate in,

00:10:50.938 --> 00:10:55.276
they could explore and visualize
their ideas in a fun and accessible way.

00:10:55.902 --> 00:10:59.655
Young people aren't typically
involved in planning spaces,

00:10:59.697 --> 00:11:03.201
but this time it was the kids
who were the experts.

00:11:03.242 --> 00:11:09.207
Just imagine all the joy, confidence
and creative ideas that leads to.

00:11:09.248 --> 00:11:11.709
And the very lovely thing here

00:11:11.751 --> 00:11:15.213
is that their vision was built
in the real world.

00:11:15.546 --> 00:11:17.256
Their ideas from the metaverse

00:11:17.298 --> 00:11:20.551
became a safe and open meeting area
in their neighborhood.

00:11:21.385 --> 00:11:28.100
(Applause)

00:11:28.142 --> 00:11:33.564
One of the kids summarized the joy
and confidence this brought

00:11:33.606 --> 00:11:36.609
in such a lovely way when she said,

00:11:36.609 --> 00:11:39.153
"Being heard and listened to

00:11:39.195 --> 00:11:41.822
is one of the best feelings you can feel."

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.869
Anytime we can include
new voices in processes

00:11:46.911 --> 00:11:48.829
where they have typically been left out,

00:11:48.829 --> 00:11:52.208
we shift dynamics, which ultimately
builds a better world.

00:11:52.708 --> 00:11:56.504
If we, in the future, have even more
metaverses on different platforms,

00:11:56.545 --> 00:11:59.674
beautiful examples like these ones
can happen even more.

00:12:00.091 --> 00:12:04.262
I hope and believe that these learnings
from the game industry

00:12:04.303 --> 00:12:06.681
and from the metaverses
the communities created

00:12:06.681 --> 00:12:10.393
truly can help us all
make better metaverses in the future.

00:12:10.726 --> 00:12:15.147
A challenge for all of us
that will design and build metaverses

00:12:15.189 --> 00:12:19.986
is to ensure that we use them
for creativity,

00:12:20.027 --> 00:12:22.571
fun, inclusivity,

00:12:22.613 --> 00:12:26.492
and ultimately to build
a better real world.

00:12:26.534 --> 00:12:27.702
Thank you so much.

00:12:27.743 --> 00:12:33.708
(Applause)

